<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Tuesday it had allocated 13.09 billion guilders to the money market under a two-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.50 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications were met for 44.7 percent.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a one-day facility of 7.74 billion guilders which expired today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsdesk +31 20 504 5000</p>
